                <pb facs="0559" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1617.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Consult if necessary with the other members of the diplomatic corps as to what
                    should be done locally to protect foreign life and property in case of a crisis.
                    Warn all Americans to remain strictly nonpartisan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
